pair G = dir(-22)*(4,1.3);
pair H = dir(-22)*(2,1);

markangle(Label("$y$",Relative(0.4)),n=1,radius=11,B,H,C);

pair X, Y;

X=A;
Y=B;
draw(1.3*X-.3*Y--1.3*Y-.3*X);

X=A;
Y=C;
draw(1.3*X-.3*Y--1.3*Y-.3*X);

X=C;
Y=B;
draw(1.3*X-.3*Y--1.3*Y-.3*X);

X=B;
Y=D;
draw(1.3*X-.3*Y--1.3*Y-.3*X);

X=G;
Y=F;
draw(1.3*X-.3*Y--1.3*Y-.3*X);

label("$n$",1.4*A-.4*B);
label("$m$",1.4*F-.4*G);

label("$50^\circ$",A+(1,-.1));
label("$90^\circ$",B+(.4,.1));
label("$40^\circ$",B+(-1,.7));
[/asy]

In rectangle $PQRS$, points $M$ and $N$ trisect $\overline{PQ}$, and points $T$ and $U$ trisect $\overline{RS}$. Additionally, $PR = PN = 3$. What is the area of quadrilateral $ABCD$ shown in the figure?

[asy]
unitsize(1cm);
pair P,M,N,Q,I,T,U,R,A,B,C,D;
P=(0,0);
M=(1,0);
N=(2,0);
Q=(3,0);
I=(3,3);
T=(2,3);
U=(1,3);
R=(0,3);
